# GuardTalkOS — laguna_rango (laguna / laguna-kernels) canonical vendor_dlkm blocklist.
#
# T-EXCISE-LAGUNA-BLOCKLIST-WIRING (P0): completes the feature-excised variant set
# by adding the laguna_rango canonical file that E-10 recorded as ABSENT, so every
# variant named in excision-variants.mk has a real file on disk.
#
# Derivation (mechanical, no invented entries):
#   upstream device/google/laguna-kernels/6.6/grapheneos/rango/vendor_dlkm.modules.blocklist
#   + GuardTalk BT-excision addition 'blocklist nitrous.ko' (T-BT-FULL FR-3, nitrous
#     BCM BT power/rfkill driver, present in vendor_dlkm.modules.load)
#   + T-EXCISE-MODEM-KERNEL additions 'blocklist cpif.ko / cpif_page.ko / shm_ipc.ko'.
# Every upstream 'blocklist' line is preserved verbatim and in order.
#
# Token-identical to vendor/guardtalk/device/rango/vendor_dlkm.modules.blocklist,
# which is the path the registry currently resolves GT_VARIANT_laguna_rango_BLOCKLIST
# to (zero-regression: rango-latest is the MVP device). This file is the canonical
# per-variant home and SHALL stay token-identical to that device copy; any future
# registry repoint must be done together with the paired Q-* gate update.
#
# Devices mapped to this variant: see excision-variants.mk GT_DEVICE_VARIANT_*.
# rango is laguna (kernel family laguna), NOT zumapro.
#
# Wi-Fi two-phase load (upstream: blocklist in the bulk pass, then re-modprobe
# without -b in init.insmod.rango.cfg) is preserved verbatim. WiFi is NOT broken.

blocklist bcmdhd4383.ko
blocklist bcmdhd4390.ko
blocklist cs40l26-i2c.ko
blocklist g_serial.ko
blocklist irq-gia-google-test.ko
blocklist sscoredump_sample_test.ko
blocklist sscoredump_test.ko
blocklist syna_touch.ko
blocklist focal_touch.ko
blocklist fst2.ko
blocklist trusty-test.ko
blocklist google_gem_test.ko
blocklist ebu-google.ko
blocklist google-cpm-tracepoint.ko

# Display
blocklist gs-panel-common-test.ko

# IOMMU
blocklist iommu_map_benchmark.ko

# T-BT-FULL (FR-3): Bluetooth power/rfkill — nitrous.ko on rango vendor_dlkm.
blocklist nitrous.ko

# T-EXCISE-MODEM-KERNEL (P0, CRIT R-2): baseband IPC transport modules — the
# kernel half of the radio airgap. cpif is the Samsung Shannon CP interface;
# cpif_page/shm_ipc are its shared-memory transport. Blocked here (honoured by
# the bulk `modprobe -b` pass) AND removed from vendor_dlkm.modules.load on the
# laguna kernels tree (grapheneos/rango) so they are neither loaded nor
# installed. Nothing boot-critical depends on any of the three (modules.dep).
# WiFi/BT unaffected (separate drivers).
blocklist cpif.ko
blocklist cpif_page.ko
blocklist shm_ipc.ko
